Known limitations (not bugs):
- The current Search is an **interim, primitive version**. Its provider (Free Dictionary API) covers ordinary words well and specialist concepts poorly, is community-run with no service guarantee, and returned HTTP 530 (unreachable) during an outage on 2026-10-24. It is planned to be replaced by Search v2.
- Search saves one item per title (matched case-insensitively); other senses are added by editing the item.
- Search text and filters reset when the app process restarts.
- UI strings are hardcoded; move to `strings.xml` before release.
- Dark-palette contrast has not been measured.
- Search recommendations setting, recent searches, and non-English lookups are not built.
- No settings are functional.
- Flashcards have no spaced repetition: study order is unreviewed first, then oldest first, or shuffled. Due counts are not shown because nothing schedules cards yet.
- The shuffle choice is not remembered between sessions (no settings storage yet).
- Study progress counts a card as reviewed when its answer is revealed; there is no "known / still learning" rating and no mastery statistic.

## 6. Decisions and Open Questions

### Confirmed product decisions
- MindVault is an Android personal knowledge app; core features are Search, Add, Vault, Flashcards.
- Users can add knowledge manually and save Search results; saved knowledge is reused across the app.
- Local-first persistence for the MVP. AI-generated content and cloud sync are out of scope.
- Package / application ID: `com.mindvault`.
- Bottom navigation order: Search, Vault, Add (center, opens a sheet), Flashcards, Home. Profile is reached from Home's top bar.
- Dark mode follows the system setting; no in-app toggle yet.
- **Search provider (interim): Free Dictionary API** (`api.dictionaryapi.dev`), no key. It sits behind `DefinitionDataSource`; switching steps are in `docs/SEARCH_PROVIDER.md`.
- **Planned Search v2 (not started):** Wiktionary for words and Wikipedia for concepts, queried in parallel, with All/Words/Concepts filters, autocomplete, ranking, compact expandable result cards, partial-failure handling, and the existing save flow unchanged. Requirements and open questions: `docs/SEARCH_V2_REQUIREMENTS.md`.
- **Flashcards & Decks (Phase 6, built, not tested):** decks are managed from the Flashcards tab and a deck screen; cards are added from the item detail screen or a picker inside a deck. Study mode takes one snapshot of the deck, with an optional shuffle that keeps your place. Reviewed = answer revealed at least once; deck complete = every card reviewed at least once. Deleting a deck or a card never deletes the Vault item. Any deck, including the default, can be renamed; only deleting the default deck is blocked.
- Search runs on the keyboard's Search action, not per keystroke.
- JSON parsing uses kotlinx.serialization (no reflection; R8-safe).

### Dependency versions
- Documented earlier: AGP 8.7.3, Gradle 8.10.2, compile/target SDK 35.
- **Observed in supplied files:** AGP 8.9.1, compile/target SDK 36. The Gradle wrapper version was not supplied and is unconfirmed (AGP 8.9 needs a newer Gradle than 8.10.2).
- Kotlin 2.0.21, KSP 2.0.21-1.0.28, Hilt 2.52, Compose BOM 2024.10.01, Navigation Compose 2.8.4, Room 2.6.1, lifecycle 2.8.7.
- Added in Phase 5 (synced and built; developer-reported): Retrofit 2.11.0, OkHttp 4.12.0, kotlinx-serialization-json 1.7.3, kotlinx-coroutines-test 1.9.0 (tests only).

